Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> Am 12.10.2011 07:02, schrieb Patric Mueller:
>> Announcing the 3.6.0 release of UnNetHack.
>> [...]
>> User Interface Improvements
>>    * Autoexplore (from AceHack)
>
> Hmm.. - doesn't that take away a elementary playing experience feature?
> (When will there be an "UN-o-matic" available? ;-)

Only after there has been a NH-o-matic. :)

Navigating the levels is not the hard part, the existing NetHack bots
already do that quite well and Vanilla NetHack is not a moving target
like UnNetHack.

>>    * stairs leading to branches are colored yellow
>
> Hmm.. - a built-in spoiler; why that?

Customer request. :)

>>    * visualized HP bar(hitpointbar) activated by default
>
> Does it require one more line on the screen or does it replace some GUI
> elements?

It is using the background behind your name and role on the first
status line with '[' and ']' added so you know where the bar ends.

It's also linked with the statuscolors patch i.e. the background
color of the hitpointbar is the same as the fourground color of your
hp display:
http://bhaak.dyndns.org/nethack/unnethack_hitpointbar.png

>
>> New Dungeon features
>>    * dead trees (from NetHack Brass)
>
> What is there use?

Mostly flavor. NetHack Brass has also floor that is colored (IIRC at
least carpet and grass) but it's more complicated to port over so I
postponed it for the time being.

>>    * Multiple bones files per level (not on Win32)
>
> Interesting. How do you merge the maps of different bones levels?

Like Benjamin said, it's not merging different bones files but having
a pool of bones files to choose from.

So you don't always get the bones files that just created for that
level.

>>    * Giantslayer grants STR 18/** when wielded
>
> Nice.

It's hard making the neglected artifacts more useful but one can try.
:)

>> More Candles
>>    * lighting shop in orcus town
>>    * Gnomes get candles (more likely in dark mines) (from AceHack)
>
> Hmm.. - the occasional too few candles in Vanilla lead to interesting
> variations; you have to be creative (or waste a wish).

Creative? Having to polymorph or pudding-farm in hope of a lucky
death-drop isn't really creative. Or do you mean something else?

> I think more (=too many) candles takes something away from the game.

The numbers certainly will be tweaked as it's likely that there are
now to many but UnNetHack already had some more source of candles like
a few in the big room and there's the possibility for an additional
lighting shop in a new branch.

>> Bug Fixes
>>    * Workaround for preventing the stairs to Vlad's tower appearing
>>      in the wizard's tower
>
> A bug from UN? (Don't know that from Vanilla.)

Yes, this is an UnNetHack bug. The new level compiler in combination
with level flipping caused it.

